INT. MARBLE FUNERAL PARLOR - DAY

Soft carpet. A hush. Wreaths of white lilies on stands. At the front, a closed mahogany coffin.

UNCLE BASIL, 60s, in a black suit, greets guests at the door. TESS, 30s, in a black dress and sunglasses, shakes his hand. MONTY, 40s, in a rumpled black suit, follows her in. ZELDA, 50s, in a veiled hat, sits in the front row, hands folded.

UNCLE BASIL
Thank you for coming. Thank you.

TESS
So sorry for your loss.

UNCLE BASIL
Thank you, dear.

TESS
(low)
He's in position.

UNCLE BASIL
(low)
Who?

TESS
Uncle Basil.

UNCLE BASIL
That's me, dear.

TESS
I know.

MONTY
(hushed)
Tess, what are you doing?

TESS
Quiet, Monty.

They walk down the aisle. Zelda turns her veiled head.

ZELDA
(whispering)
Tess. Monty. Sit.

They sit. Zelda leans in.

ZELDA (CONT'D)
(to Monty)
Is everything in place?

MONTY
Everything's in place.

ZELDA
(to Tess)
And the vault?

TESS
Monty has the vault.

MONTY
I have the vault.

ZELDA
Good. When the organ starts, you move.

TESS
And Uncle Basil?

ZELDA
Basil is the one who's dead.

Tess blinks. Monty chokes.

MONTY
Uncle Basil is at the door.

ZELDA
That is Basil's twin. Basilius. They've been swapping for decades.

TESS
Then who's in the coffin?

ZELDA
The plan.

The organ begins. A slow, mournful hymn. Everyone in the room stands. Zelda lifts her veil, revealing a very small smile.

ZELDA (CONT'D)
(whispering)
Now.

The coffin lid opens by itself.
